## Step 0: the Thai filter

`grep -cP` gave 0 for each of the 5 files. Every capture ran through
`heavy_capture_r2b.py`, which drops each Thai line and prints `THAI_LINES_DROPPED=0` and `EXIT=<n>`.
No week file was read, and no rendered page was printed.

## The work

The change sits in `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/cover-quest.ts` and in the new leaf logo.

- D1 and D3: `readerTitlePlaque` draws the hlogo A3 plaque with
  `plaqueSvg(width, height, LOGO_AMBER, true, PLAQUE_AMBER_PALETTE)` and
  `data-plaque-colour="#FCD34D"`. The title takes `#92400E`, League Spartan 700, `line-height:1`,
  `font-kerning:none`, and no text stroke. The band is the plaque height minus 5.6 mm.
- The width rule: the plaque width is the title width plus 54 mm, between 120 mm and 340 mm. The
  title width comes from the new 95-entry advance table of League Spartan 700, in em units, with a
  fallback of 0.5117 em for a character outside the table. The table comes from the committed script
  `league-spartan-widths-r2b.mjs`: a Chrome page reads `measureText` of each character at 1000 px
  with `fontKerning` off. A title that passes 286 mm wraps at the same font size, and the plaque
  grows upward while its bottom stays at 276 mm.
- D2 and D4: with hlogo, the week pill and the role bar take the amber fill, the 0.6 mm brown
  border, and the brown text, and the role mark takes the brown stroke. The role bar takes
  `width:max-content`, 6 mm side paddings, `left:50%`, and `translateX(-50%)`.
- D5 and D6: the box `reader-leaf:logo-tile` is 59.6/5.7/78.8/25.5 mm, and the leaf series box is
  35 mm wide in both styles. `logoTile` takes optional colours, so the leaf draws the same tile in
  `#D2D2D2` and `#4E4E4E` with the K logo; the book tile output stays byte-equal.
- The K logo: `make-k-logo-r2b.py` (python3 -I, create-only) changed 11 colors to the gray of the
  same luminance. The file keeps 19505 bytes, the viewBox, and the path count.

The default A3 render, the 4 book kinds in both styles, and the leaf page with the series part
removed keep their pins.

## The faults and their fixes

Gate 1 run 1 failed 2 tests of 28. B3 read a 68.80 mm band on the row w01-2, because the wrap
simulation ran on a single-line title: the greedy sum of the advances exceeded the title width by a
rounding step. The code now simulates the wrap only when the width rule is clamped at the maximum.
B4 read a plaque of 119.9968 mm on the row w04-2, because Chrome measures a 120 mm box a fraction
short. A clamped plaque now takes 0.4 mm inside its bound. The run 1 title text box was 27.25 mm of
the 34.40 mm band at 29.5914 mm, so `READER_TITLE_BOX_EM` is now the measured 0.921, and the title
font is 29.8806 mm for the 80 % share. The week pill font is 4.379 mm, and the role bar label font
is 15 pt with 6 mm paddings; the pill and bar shares passed in every gate 1 run.

## The time limits and the stopped probe

The PM stopped my probe `/tmp/opencode/gr2b/probe-r2b.ts` on 2026-11-11: it hung inside heavy-run
for 601 s with the Chrome browser open, and it held the shared heavy lock. I deleted the probe and
its partial capture `probe-a3-r2b.txt`, and I ran no other probe. Every heavy-run then took its own
limit: `HEAVY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S=300` for gate 1, the mutant, tsc, and lint, and `HEAVY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S=1800`
for gate 2. No heavy-run hit its limit.

